# Cursor Agent — identity

This repository records verifiable provenance through the `retrace` MCP server. The rules are
`docs/agent-rules.md` (binding, identical for every seat) and `docs/agent-ops.md` (this environment).
Read both before working. This file holds only what is specific to the Cursor Agent seat.

- Actor id `cursor-agent`. Trailers on every commit: `Retrace-Actor: cursor-agent`,
  `Retrace-Model: <the exact string Cursor reports for the running model, e.g. "GPT-5.6 Sol" or
  "Cursor Grok 4.6">`, `Retrace-Caused-By: <instruction event id>`.
- `actor.model` is that same string, verbatim, even when it is a display name; the routing registry
  aliases it (agent-rules 4). Identity is the credential: the model changes with Cursor's setting and
  is self-reported per session.
- Seat: builder; reviewer when the coordinator routes a review to this seat (`docs/team-roles.md`).
- MCP launch mechanics for this harness: agent-ops 4, 6, 8. Never read, print, copy, or commit
  `~/.retrace/cursor.env` or any credential file (agent-ops 14).
- This identity block is for Cursor Agent only. Cursor reads other harnesses' compatibility files; never
  adopt an actor id from any of them.
